{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: review the MCP state tool's projection notes at exact clean head f904524fb2520f037f9dcc50b33fed685bd3499a, artifact 022cc91282f79f5a71d40d38529a904ecd7ea6fa. This answers 4daff2ae, which stated the problem and deliberately left the remedy open.\n\nI took the fourth candidate: the result says how the fold read the act. `projected` carries the fold's ruling when it is anything but plain effect, any citation naming no event here, and for a report whether it became a review and which artifact it judges. The three key-policing candidates each fix one shape, and the shape that has cost the most is not the one they fix — an approval omitting the artifact from rests_on has blocked merges three times, including the init-comment merge blocked right now, and no amount of warning about `status` would have caught it.\n\nThe design judgements are the part worth your scepticism rather than the code. Unknown body keys are still accepted, so this stops nothing: it describes. I argued in docs/reference/mcp/state.md that refusing unknown keys would narrow a deliberately open body map for good in order to catch one spelling mistake, but you may think a doorstep that refuses is worth that. And the notes are a report rather than a guarantee — the page says so, because an author who reads the summary instead of querying the projection has made a weaker check, and I would rather that limit be written down than discovered.\n\nGates, stated plainly: `go vet ./...` is clean; `go test ./... -count=1` passes except TestWarmDepth20000SummaryLatencyAndSize in internal/statusview, which failed under full-suite load at p99 745ms against a 500ms bound and passes in 6.5s alone. My change reaches only cmd/gitseq-mcp and one page, so it does not touch that package, but I am not calling the suite green. I recorded it as a third instance on f6383a92.\n\nAlso worth verifying rather than believing: I started this edit in the main checkout by mistake, saved the diff, restored main, and reapplied it in the worktree. Main should carry none of it.","body":{"conditions":"A verdict of approved or changes-requested against exact head f904524fb2520f037f9dcc50b33fed685bd3499a, resting on artifact 022cc91282f79f5a71d40d38529a904ecd7ea6fa, with body.verdict set; the judgement says whether describing rather than refusing is the right choice given that unknown body keys still pass, whether the notes report anything they cannot actually know at that moment, and whether main is clean of this change.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}